	<h2>The Zero-Trust Editorial Mandate</h2>
	<p>
		The <strong>ErrorLedger Editorial Team</strong> enforces a strict, zero-trust framework for compiling our analysis database. We do not aggregate generic blog posts or rewrite press releases. Our mandate is to extract actionable, structural truths by analyzing the lowest-level primary documentation available.
	</p>

	<h2>The Primary Sourcing Hierarchy</h2>
	<p>
		To prevent speculation and misinformation, every analysis in our database is graded on a rigid primary-source hierarchy:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Grade A — Systematic Reviews & Meta-Analyses:</strong> Cochrane Reviews, PRISMA-compliant meta-analyses, and multi-study syntheses with quantified effect sizes and confidence intervals.</li>
		<li><strong>Grade B — Controlled Empirical Evidence & Primary Specs:</strong> Peer-reviewed Randomized Controlled Trials (RCTs in <em>The Journal of Physiology</em>, <em>Nature</em>, <em>Lancet</em>), official vendor post-mortems (RCAs), and primary RFC/architecture specifications.</li>
		<li><strong>Grade C — Documented Architecture & Public Disclosures:</strong> Open-source repository architecture documentation, SEC filings, and audited security CVE reports.</li>
		<li><strong>Grade D/E — Benchmarks & Industry Telemetry:</strong> Large-scale reproducible benchmarks (>1,000 runs/subjects) and verified telemetry datasets.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Our Systems Audit Pipeline</h2>
	<p>
		We process raw technical and physiological data through a multi-stage editorial convergence pipeline:
	</p>
	<ol>
		<li><strong>Scope & Baseline Definition:</strong> We establish the exact operating environment, target population, and time horizons under review.</li>
		<li><strong>Mechanism vs. Reality Extraction:</strong> We isolate the claimed mechanism and evaluate it against physical or biological laws to expose core failure modes, race conditions, or anabolic signaling trade-offs.</li>
		<li><strong>Facts vs. Inference Demarcation:</strong> Every statement is explicitly labeled as an <em>Observed Fact</em>, <em>Documented Specification</em>, or <em>Engineering/Systemic Inference</em>.</li>
		<li><strong>Operational Diagnostic Tools:</strong> We package validated diagnostic tools (Python calculators, Prometheus alerting rules, and log parsers) for instant practical utility.</li>
		<li><strong>Automated Self-Healing QA Audit:</strong> Before publication, our automated audit engine scans the draft for linguistic absolutes, pseudo-exact generalizations, and evidentiary integrity.</li>
	</ol>

	<h2>Zero Absolutes Policy</h2>
	<p>
		ErrorLedger strictly prohibits dogmatic assertions. We never publish claims that a tool or intervention "always works" or "completely eliminates failure." Instead, we provide probabilistic, constraint-aware evaluations so engineers, researchers, and practitioners can make informed decisions.
	</p>
